{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"The promise diagnostics resolved the leader-side question but left one point open: with the StopSign holders and node 3 all reporting accepted 37, the receipt could not say whether node 3's position 37 is the StopSign or whether the decision at 38 refers to a position node 3 never accepted. is_reconfigured() answers that directly, since Some means the log holds an accepted StopSign and None means it does not. This revision keeps the seeded 900-action schedule, reconfigure at action 450, 150-round convergence, node 3 ordered trace, node 4 promise diagnostics and the converged_all comparison unchanged, and adds n3_reconfig and n4_reconfig to the safety event, encoded as 0 for None, 1 for Some(false) and 2 for Some(true). If node 3 reports a StopSign while the leader decided 38, the stall is not a missing AcceptStopSign at all: node 3 would hold the reconfiguration marker and be unable to accept the later position that others decided, which would reclassify the case under the StopSign-clearing family rather than the sequence-clamp family. If node 3 reports no StopSign, the original reading stands and the clamping Decides are what block it. Either way the progress loss stays established.\"}"}}
